WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.960 --> 00:00:06.080
A new stream of lava has begun flowing&nbsp;
from the volcano erupting on the Spanish&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:06.080 --> 00:00:10.160
island of La Palma. The lava is&nbsp;
threatening to engulf more homes&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:10.160 --> 00:00:14.160
in addition to the hundreds that have&nbsp;
already been damaged or destroyed. But&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:14.160 --> 00:00:18.160
while the volcano is posing a&nbsp;
serious danger to lives and property,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:18.160 --> 00:00:23.600
it's also attracting visitors to the island eager&nbsp;
to see the spectacle of a volcano in action.&nbsp;

00:00:27.280 --> 00:00:33.120
Thousands have fled from its destructive force,&nbsp;
but others are attracted. The erupting Cumbre&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:33.120 --> 00:00:38.880
Vieja is now another tourist attraction on&nbsp;
this holiday isle. Some have traveled to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:38.880 --> 00:00:45.280
snap a selfie with an erupting volcano.
"It is a once in a life time opportunity&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:45.280 --> 00:00:50.960
to see something like this and we just thought it&nbsp;
worth make the journey. So we got the ferry across&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:50.960 --> 00:00:53.520
in it's absolutely fantastic. It's very sad&nbsp;
seeing the lava going down here because it&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:53.520 --> 00:00:58.000
looks like it might, it's destroying quite a&nbsp;
lot more houses. But still, it's good to see&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:58.000 --> 00:01:01.920
the natural beauty of this."
"It is incredible,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:01.920 --> 00:01:05.840
there is lot of noise, it is the&nbsp;
power and the beauty of the volcano."&nbsp;

00:01:08.880 --> 00:01:12.720
But many island residents are wishing&nbsp;
for an end to the instability.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:13.360 --> 00:01:17.120
Thousands have been forced to&nbsp;
evacuate, some have lost everything.&nbsp;

00:01:19.520 --> 00:01:29.120
"The land I had is all gone. The inheritance I had&nbsp;
there. The memories of my parents. It's all gone."&nbsp;

00:01:31.920 --> 00:01:38.960
Lava continues to devour properties. The moving&nbsp;
molten mass has consumed more than a thousand&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:38.960 --> 00:01:45.520
buildings in the three weeks since eruptions&nbsp;
began, setting fire to everything in its path.&nbsp;

00:01:49.840 --> 00:01:55.520
Recent nights have seen fresh flows from&nbsp;
the fiery mountain, as the unstable cone&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:55.520 --> 00:02:01.520
collapses and new fissures appear, sending&nbsp;
rivers of magma in different directions.&nbsp;

00:02:02.960 --> 00:02:07.840
Cumbre Vieja shows no sign of settling down.

